          </div>

          <div class="ch-pane active" data-pane="overview">
            <p>
              Sales reps in the field order without signal. Orders queue on-device with idempotency
              keys and sync safely when the network returns, with no duplicates and no lost work. The app
              tracks customer visits and stock counts, and closes the day with reports: sales
              history with order-status breakdowns, end-of-day summaries, and activity maps.
            </p>
            <div class="arc-tags">
              <span>Next.js (PWA)</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>Tailwind CSS</span><span>IndexedDB sync queue</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ch-pane" data-pane="flow">
            <div class="flow-strip">
              <div class="flow-node"><b>01 DEVICE</b><span>Order saved to IndexedDB + UUID key</span></div>
              <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">➜</span>
              <div class="flow-node warn"><b>02 DEAD ZONE</b><span>Queued safely offline · zero data loss</span></div>
              <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">➜</span>
              <div class="flow-node ok"><b>03 ONLINE SYNC</b><span>Idempotent POST · no duplicate orders</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="ch-pane" data-pane="code">
            <div class="manga-term compact">
              <div class="term-head" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="term-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
                <span class="term-title">CHAPTER_01.TS // オフライン同期</span>
              </div>
              <pre class="code">// Concept — a stable idempotency key rides with every queued order,
// so a retry after a flaky network can never create a duplicate.
queue.enqueue('order.create', order.withIdempotencyKey());</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

